{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"05b642faa230e034","type":"text","text":"Maybe a small scene with Jane & Sara talking about how it looks like there won't be a third pregnancy, but they're thankful that they have their own children.\n\nMaybe with Emma being a young adult, and Anne will be one before too long, they wonder about grandchildren. \n\nI just picturing this certain smile from Sara. Years ago she didn't expect to have any children of her own, now she's wondering about grandchildren. ","x":-300,"y":-280,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"0c86b39f4ff1f95b","x":240,"y":-280,"width":400,"height":400,"type":"text","text":"Heck I could even have a scene at some point maybe when Emma is a teenager or something, Sara and Jane are talking about how they've been trying for a third pregnancy for years now but it doesn't seem like it's going to happen. And they're basically just like well at least we got these three girls. Like basically the two of them accepting that it's not going to happen. "},
		{"id":"c65759af5672593e","x":-300,"y":200,"width":400,"height":400,"type":"text","text":"Yes, adoption was an option, but there's something about having her own kids. Sara always had a preference there. "}
	],
	"edges":[]
}